source: crates/daemon/tests/integration/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Give an action its own keys in the TUI and the web app, in keys.toml. Writes nothing when a key belongs to another action

Usage: mxr keys set [OPTIONS] <ACTION> [KEYS]...

Arguments:
  <ACTION>   The action id, such as mail.archive; `mxr keys` lists them
  [KEYS]...  Its keys, primary first, spelled as `mxr keys` prints them

Options:
      --none               Leave the action without a key; the palette still runs it
      --dry-run            Show the change and any conflict; write nothing
      --client <CLIENT>    Only this client's keys [possible values: tui, web]
      --context <CONTEXT>  Only keys live in this place: a TUI context or web scope, such as todo
      --format <FORMAT>    [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]
  -h, --help               Print help
